WEBVTT

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.000
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.800
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.430
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.140
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.140
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.430
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.430
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.290
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.460
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:34.490
Last week, after Eggman was defeated by Sonic, he sank into the ocean. However...

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.740
We can't find him!

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.370
We can't find him!

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:42.870
You can't find him?

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:49.210
He's most likely hiding at the bottom of the ocean.

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:52.960
There's no way Eggman has given up!

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:54.260
Find him!

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.310
I've recently been working all the time without a break.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:13.900
I want to go to the beach for vacation.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:35.340
Umm...

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:36.550
You idiot!

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:41.430
Don't make a sound. Or else, the military search teams will find us.

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:44.720
We have to stay quiet until they're finished.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:45.680
Right.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.910
Start repairing the ship again!

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:09.580
Roger!

00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:12.040
That's a lot of work...

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:18.610
Episode 16

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:18.610
Aim for it! The Sunken Ship in the Southern Seas

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.430
Let's review what we learned last time.

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.810
Do you remember which fork and knife to use?

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.060
Leave it to me!

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:29.520
These!

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.810
Correct! You all remember!

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:34.610
You're good children!

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:38.730
Everyone's here.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:40.190
What's up, Chuck?

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:45.410
We're going to give you important documents, so carefully look over them.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:46.780
Documents?

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.080
What are these?

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:54.130
Your Social Security card and passport.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:04:01.170
Tails, you also get a special airplane pilot license, airplane mechanic license and others.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:03.180
These are all mine?

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.390
That's a lot of documents, Tails.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:10.270
If you keep on flying without a license, you will be arrested.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:14.980
However, with those licenses, you can fly anywhere in this country.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.110
Chuck.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:20.990
What kind of license is this for Cheese?

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:28.160
That certifies that Cheese is the honorary citizen Cream's pet.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.330
What? A pet?

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:38.170
How rude! Cheese is not my pet! Cheese is my dear friend!

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:41.880
Calm down... Don't be like that.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:44.340
Make sure to cancel this!

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.050
Okay, okay.

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:47.930
What?

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.430
What's this!

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:52.180
What?

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:52.980
Let me see.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:53.930
What's wrong?

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:58.770
Didn't they have a cuter picture of me?

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:03.690
They probably used a photo that a newspaper reporter secretly took.

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:08.870
Why did they have to use such a bad photo?

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:10.830
I can't stand it!

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:14.580
Hey guys! It looks like you're having a lot of fun.

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:18.000
Sonic, you came at a good time.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:20.130
Here. This is yours, Sonic.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:22.050
What's this?

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:26.340
It's called a passport, and it allows you to go to other countries.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:29.430
Other countries?

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:34.310
I already did run all around this country...

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:36.770
Sounds interesting!

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:44.740
Goodbye.

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:46.610
Bye bye.

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:49.820
Yes, bye bye.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:54.160
Bye, Grandpa.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:57.080
Be careful.

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:06.470
X-Tornado, taking off!

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:20.650
Goodbye! Take care!

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:27.950
Tanaka, nothing bad must happen to Chris on this trip.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:28.740
Understood.

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:30.320
Leave it to me.

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:44.090
Amy, where are we all going?

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:49.170
How about here? Grand Blue Sapphire Sea.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:53.930
The deep blue waters, white walls, a balcony with an ocean view...

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.600
How wonderfully romantic.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:59.350
Amy, can you hear me?

00:07:01.480 --> 00:07:04.980
Look down. The ocean is really beautiful!

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:08.690
No good. Don't settle for a place so nearby.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:11.820
My heart is already set on Grand Blue.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:17.450
But we're flying over Grand Blue Sapphire Sea right now.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.340
It's too beautiful.

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:32.340
It's wonderful.

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:38.350
I've decided this is the place. Hurry up and land!

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:39.770
Hurry!

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:43.150
Right.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:44.400
Chris!

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:46.070
What's up?

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:47.610
The Chaos Emerald.

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:52.610
The Emerald is glowing.

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:55.910
What's going on?

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:03.210
This also happened at Diamond Stadium. Which means...

00:08:03.370 --> 00:08:07.290
The fourth Chaos Emerald is somewhere around here.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:08.670
The fourth...

00:08:09.130 --> 00:08:10.710
Chaos Emerald.

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:16.550
Hang on tight, everyone! We're going to land!

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:27.730
We're finally here. Let's see...

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.690
Lets go to the beach for now.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:34.030
Isn't that Sonic?

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.780
What? Sonic? No way!

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:37.410
It's really Sonic!

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:47.000
What?

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:48.710
Not again.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.300
Run away for now!

00:09:00.430 --> 00:09:03.430
We're the center of attention no matter where we go.

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:09.310
With all those stares, I'd rather sneak around than walk with our heads held high.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.280
How troublesome.

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:14.950
Maybe it was better if we pretended to be stuffed animals.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:17.410
It can't be helped. You're famous.

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:21.080
Well, let's change into our swimsuits.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:22.540
Huh?

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:26.080
Where did Sonic go?

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:26.960
Huh?

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:30.750
Don't tell me he went ahead to search for the Emerald by himself?

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:37.720
Hey, Sonic! Hey!

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:41.560
Sonic, where did you go?

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:43.060
I'm over here.

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:46.520
There you are.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:48.900
What are you doing here?

00:09:54.690 --> 00:10:00.370
I'm thinking of a way to search for the Chaos Emerald that's under the sea.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:07.920
All we have to do is find a way to stay underwater for a long period of time.

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:09.630
Leave it to me!

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:12.630
Yay!

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:13.960
Here's to you!

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:19.680
This is the best!

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:23.350
Crab.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:27.100
Sonic, put this in your mouth.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.980
Is this really going to work?

00:10:31.880 --> 00:10:36.880
<i>Sign: Good kids won't try this at home!</i>

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:36.440
It will! With this, you'll be able to breathe underwater.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:39.450
All you have to do is walk slowly.

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:40.890
<i>Sign: You mean I'm not a good kid?</i>

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:41.030
Walk?

00:10:41.450 --> 00:10:43.410
Okay, I'll try.

00:10:43.740 --> 00:10:45.120
Give it your best shot, Sonic.

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:28.950
Sonic...

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:31.960
Oh, you're back.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:34.670
What do you think you're doing, you crab!

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:41.130
Sonic, you'll be fine this time.

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:43.180
No problem.

00:11:43.490 --> 00:11:47.040
<i>Sign: Do not imitate</i>

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:46.560
Where did you bring that from?

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:59.690
I can breathe, but I can't see ahead!

00:12:00.110 --> 00:12:01.490
Sheesh.

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:08.330
It's dark! It's cramped! Chris, pull me up! Pull me up!

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:11.660
I thought I was going to die.

00:12:12.000 --> 00:12:15.330
Oh, come on. It's not that easy to die.

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:21.510
I guess if we're going to dive into the ocean, we should use diving gear.

00:12:21.760 --> 00:12:24.590
It's dangerous to use equipment that's not meant for diving.

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:26.850
You should have done that in the first place!

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:45.570
How much will it cost to rent diving suits for everyone and a boat?

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:47.570
You don't need to pay.

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:56.170
Congress passed a special Sonic budget, so the country will pay for everything.

00:12:58.170 --> 00:13:00.920
By the way, what are you planning to do by renting a boat?

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:04.630
Well... Umm...

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:09.680
Hey! This model boat is the same as the one in the picture.

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.220
Yes it is.

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:19.020
That's the legendary boat that sunk long ago in the Grand Blue Sapphire Sea.

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:23.030
During the Age of Exploration, a storm struck the ship.

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:29.620
Everybody, let's go.

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:32.700
Goodbye and good luck.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:36.790
Bon voyage.

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:40.500
Tails and I will watch over Sonic.

00:13:40.540 --> 00:13:41.500
Thank you.

00:13:41.500 --> 00:13:43.550
Practice swimming a little.

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:47.800
Breathe slowly when you're underwater.

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:48.800
Okay.

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:49.850
Here I go.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:56.350
Let's go.

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:57.980
Yeah...

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:33.640
We finally finished the repairs.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:35.470
It was a lot of work.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:36.980
I'm exhausted.

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:47.070
The famous Sonic is currently enjoying his vacation at the Grand Blue Sapphire Sea.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:51.620
What? A vacation?

00:14:51.620 --> 00:14:55.870
On the other hand, we're covered in oil and soot and having a rough time.

00:14:55.910 --> 00:14:59.080
While they're having a wonderful vacation.

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:02.380
I'm so jealous!

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:07.010
That punk Sonic!

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:15.470
The signal from the Chaos Emerald is getting stronger.

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:18.060
That's...

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:25.320
This is...

00:15:30.150 --> 00:15:35.160
Isn't this the ship that the diving shop owner was talking about?

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:38.330
I wonder if the Chaos Emerald is inside.

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:41.420
Let's search inside.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:49.550
I found them!

00:15:57.220 --> 00:15:58.140
Huh?

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:04.650
Sonic's not here. Only the pipsqueak is here. Why?

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:12.280
I guess it won't hurt to take a small vacation.

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:17.700
I'm back.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:24.620
Good job. I hope you relayed my message to Sonic.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:26.250
Yes!

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:31.880
Having a good time, Sonic? How dare you go on vacation!

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:39.350
Thanks to you, I'm having a horrible time. Just wait. I promise to make you pay!

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:39.350
<i>This is the message I sent to Sonic.</i>

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:44.230
Why are you showing this to me? Did you really relay this message to Sonic?

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:48.730
Sonic wasn't there. Only a pipsqueak.

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:51.320
So I had no choice but to bring it back.

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:55.570
This message will now automatically self-destruct.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:00.580
I rigged the device to explode.

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:02.700
Which means...

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:12.670
That hedgehog punk! Let's go!

00:17:13.510 --> 00:17:16.010
I'm really going to make him pay this time.

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:22.890
Wow!

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:26.100
It's beautiful.

00:17:27.270 --> 00:17:29.110
It's sparkling.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:32.070
The whole ship is like a jewel box.

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:39.070
The signal from the Chaos Emerald is becoming even stronger. A new Emerald may be mixed in with the treasure.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:42.080
Yeah, you're probably right.

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:45.620
What?

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:50.090
That's...

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:52.300
The Chaos Emerald.

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:54.010
It was here after all.

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:57.430
Hey!

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:59.180
We meet again.

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:02.720
Huh, crab.

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:09.650
It ran away!

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:13.650
Is this the fourth Chaos Emerald?

00:18:13.940 --> 00:18:16.030
Fantastic!

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:18.320
I found you, hedgehog!

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.290
So this is where you were.

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:29.750
Go, E-57!

00:18:31.880 --> 00:18:35.800
Everyone, escape to the surface! I'll fight him!

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:39.590
Understood. Everyone, let's hurry!

00:18:55.110 --> 00:18:59.320
I can't run well underwater. I'm barely managing to dodge the attacks!

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:03.330
All right! Finish him, E-57!

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:12.580
I love things like this!

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:15.670
There you go.

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:17.300
No one's hurt, right?

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:18.590
Yeah, we're all fine.

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:21.890
Chris!

00:19:24.140 --> 00:19:25.930
So you're safe!

00:19:26.970 --> 00:19:27.970
Tanaka!

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:32.690
Please hurry and come aboard this boat.

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:35.400
Tanaka, why are you here?

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:40.030
My job is to keep you safe at all times.

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:44.990
Therefore, when danger approaches you, I will always come.

00:20:07.140 --> 00:20:09.390
Stop playing with me!

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:11.640
Stop!

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:13.100
Sonic is...

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:21.070
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:22.700
Uncle!

00:20:23.410 --> 00:20:26.450
Call me High Speed Big Wave today!

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:32.210
Grab this, supersonic guy!

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:36.040
Here we go!

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:39.380
All right!

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:42.970
Just watch!

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:49.600
Your lame missiles can't hit me.

00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:53.810
Sonic!

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:57.650
Sonic, take this!

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.080
He did it!

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:26.180
Thank you.

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:33.390
You found a sunken ship off the shore?

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:41.320
Yes, but Eggman destroyed it, so there's nothing left of the ship or the treasure.

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:43.650
I see...

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:47.780
But you really did see the sunken ship.

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:48.870
Yes.

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:53.370
So the story wasn't made up.

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:56.370
The legend was true.

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:09.510
It turns out that the captain of the sunken ship was the ancestor of the owner of the diving shop.

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:14.810
What a beautiful sunset.

00:22:16.350 --> 00:22:19.600
I finally feel like we're on vacation.

00:22:27.780 --> 00:22:35.580
Although Dr. Eggman appeared at the Grand Blue Sapphire Sea today, thanks to the Sonic team-

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:40.830
I hate him!

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:54.450
<b>Watashitachi no sekai wa mahou o kakerarete</b>

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:54.450
<i>There’s magic cast on our world.</i>

00:22:54.450 --> 00:23:03.420
<b>Ai suru to kime kisae namida ni ujirareteru</b>

00:22:54.450 --> 00:23:03.420
<i>The nervousness of love is sealed by tears.</i>

00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:12.300
<b>Boy boy futari de jumon wo sagashi ni ikou</b>

00:23:03.420 --> 00:23:12.300
<i>Boy, let’s search for a spell together,</i>

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:21.900
<b>Kinji rareta yume wo kanaerareru kuni he</b>

00:23:12.300 --> 00:23:21.900
<i>To a land where our forbidden dreams can come true.</i>

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:30.840
<b>Dare ni mo naisho de ashita na tchi awaseshiyou</b>

00:23:22.770 --> 00:23:30.840
<i>Let’s secretly meet tomorrow.</i>

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:41.040
<b>Itsuka kotori wo ume ta yowake no mieru oka de</b>

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:41.040
<i>At the place where we buried the bird, the hill where we can see the sunrise.</i>

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:49.800
<b>Tsumetai asamoya kimi to te wo tsunaidara</b>

00:23:41.620 --> 00:23:49.800
<i>In the cold morning mist, if I hold hands with you.</i>

00:23:50.550 --> 00:23:58.970
<b>Hikaru michi no fuuin ga tokeru yo</b>

00:23:50.550 --> 00:23:58.970
<i>The seal to the shining path will be broken.</i>

00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:03.810
<b>Hateshinaku</b>

00:23:59.520 --> 00:24:03.810
<i>Forever...</i>

00:24:30.510 --> 00:25:35.360
Knuckles! Clenched Fists of Anger
